cutefish-meta (26.04.6) resolute; urgency=medium

  * cutefish-live: OpenSnitch rule allowing the installer and the programs it
    runs in the new system, so its geoip and connectivity checks and the
    online ubuntu-drivers step don't wait on prompts. Purged with
    cutefish-live after the install.

 -- Cutefish Remastered <remastered@localhost>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:42:50 +0600

cutefish-meta (26.04.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * cutefish-live: quote the installer autostart Exec with double quotes.
    Single quotes are not quoting in desktop entries (or QProcess::
    splitCommand), so the session ran sh -c "'grep" and the installer never
    opened by itself.
  * calamares-settings-cutefish: depend on cracklib-runtime; without its
    dictionary the users page said "The password fails the dictionary check -
    error loading dictionary" for every password.
  * calamares-settings-cutefish: depend on rsync. Calamares' unpackfs copies
    the live system with it and calamares doesn't depend on it, so every
    install failed with "rsync failed with error code 127".
  * calamares-logs-helper: save the journal as the installer's syslog. There
    is no /var/log/syslog, and the failed cp ended every install with
    "External command finished with errors".

 -- Cutefish Remastered <remastered@localhost>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:03:41 +0600

